# Frosthollow: the mining town in a high snowy valley in the Whitefangs, up the pass road. The Frozen Lantern, the
# smithy and the smelter, the general store, the chapel, the healer, the mines above the town, the slag heap, the
# snow and the cold, and the ore carts down the pass. Lord Aldric Grayrock of Ridgemere is on his way up to the mines.

scene rg_cb_nail_shrine
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Knocked a nail into the mine door this morning. Another safe week. | The mine door's more nail than wood now. | My father's nails are in that door still. Hundreds of them.
b[miner] : A nail for every return. Forget one and the mountain forgets you.
b[priest] : The Bright One counts every return. Nails or no nails.
b : Long may it last. | Lot of safe returns. | Good wolf, your father.
a : Long may it. | Lots, thank the Bright One. | He was.

scene rg_cb_pit_songs
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : The old pit songs keep time with the picks. | Sang the lamp song all the way down this morning. | My grandmother taught me the shaft song. Nobody knows the last verse.
b[miner] : Sing below, and you know the wolf beside you is still breathing.
b[old] : The last verse is for the ones who didn't come up. You only sing it in the chapel.
b : They do. | Good for luck. | Somebody must.
a : Every stroke. | Always. | Somebody must.

scene rg_cb_taste_ore
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow a.job=miner|smith|laborer
a : Taste that. Good ore. You can tell by the bite. | This seam's gone sour. Tastes of copper. | The iron vein's back, rich as blood.
b[miner] : Old miners taste the rock. New ones lick their lamps.
b[smith] : Good ore makes my anvil sing. Bring it.
b : I'll take your word. | Bad luck. | Finally.
a : Wise. | Very bad. | Finally.

scene rg_cb_lamp_all_night
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow here.time=dusk|night
a : I keep a lamp lit all night. Can't sleep in the dark any more. | Every window in the miners' row has a lamp in it. | Lamp oil's half my wages.
b[miner] : After a day below, darkness feels like the shaft again.
b[old] : The lamps used to be for the ones still down. Now it's just habit.
b : I understand. | Pretty, on the snow. | Mine too.
a : Thank you. | It is. | Everyone's.

scene rg_cb_cough
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Everybody coughs in Frosthollow. Blame the cold. | My cough's worse in winter. | Even the children cough here.
b[healer] : It's not the cold. It's the dust. Wear a cloth over your muzzle.
b[old] : Coughed fifty years. Still here.
b : The cold. Of course. | Everyone's is. | It's the smelter smoke.
a : Of course. | Everyone's. | The smoke.

scene rg_cb_north_seam
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Nobody works the north seam since the lights. | They say the north seam groans at night. | Three wolves died in the north seam in my grandfather's day.
b[miner] : The north seam is cursed. I won't go near it. Nobody should.
b[priest] : There is no curse but carelessness. Pray, and prop your timbers.
b : Wise of them. | Settling rock. | I'd heard two.
a : Very wise. | Probably. | Three.

scene rg_cb_trapped
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow pair.band=friends|family|acquaintances
a : Old Ember was trapped two days below. Won't go down any more. | They dug the Flint brothers out after a day. One of them still won't talk. | Ever think about getting trapped?
b[miner] : Every time I go down. Every single time.
b[healer] : Two days below changes a wolf. Be gentle with them.
b : Who'd blame him? | Poor soul. | I try not to.
a : Nobody. | Poor soul. | Me neither.

scene rg_cb_crown_price
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : The ore buyers' price is theft. Plain theft. | The buyer's man was weighing carts again. | We dig, Ridgemere gets rich. Same as always.
b[miner] : Let the buyers come down a shaft and then name a price.
b[merchant] : The price is fair for the times. The road down eats the rest.
b : It is. | Weighing them light, no doubt. | Same as always.
a : Plain theft. | No doubt. | Always.

scene rg_cb_sister_city
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow pair.band=friends|family|spouses|acquaintances
a : I send half my wage to my sister in Ridgemere. | My cousin moved down to the city. Never writes. | Ridgemere's only down the pass and along the High Road, but it's another world.
b[old] : The city eats the young ones. Always has.
b : Good of you. | They never do. | It is.
a : She's family. | Never. | Another world.

scene rg_cb_hot_anvil
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow here.place=tavern
a : Fight at the Frozen Lantern last night over the shift roster. | Miners' boots lined up at the Lantern door like soldiers. | Ash in my ale again.
b[innkeeper] : Loudest inn in the Whitefangs. I'm proud of it.
b[miner] : The roster's a crime. Somebody had to say it.
b : Again? | Every night. | Drink it anyway.
a : Again. | Every night. | I did.

scene rg_cb_charcoal
when topic=work|lore here.region=frosthollow
a : The charcoal burners came in black as night. | Smoke from the clamps on the ridge. | The smelter eats charcoal faster than the burners can make it.
b[laborer] : Sat by a clamp for three nights. Can't smell anything now.
b[smith] : No charcoal, no iron. Simple as that.
b : Every time. | Thick today. | They always do.
a : Every time. | Very thick. | Always.

scene rg_cb_bonesetter
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : The healer set three legs this week. | The bench at the healer's is never empty. | Got my paw splinted after the rockfall. Still aches.
b[healer] : Bones knit. Lungs don't. Wear your muzzle cloth.
b : Bad week. | Never. | It will.
a : Very bad. | Never. | For a while.

scene rg_cb_red_dust
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Everything's grey here. My fur, my bread, even the snow. | Washed my coat three times. Still grey. | You can tell a Frosthollow wolf in the city by the grey in their fur.
b[child] : I'm grey all over! Look!
b[old] : The grey never comes out. You get used to it.
b : That's the smelter. | It never comes out. | Proud of it.
a : The smelter. | Never. | Very proud.

scene rg_cb_forge_orders
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow a.job=smith|apprentice|laborer
a : Picks and wedges, picks and wedges. Every day. | The city wants a cartload of bar iron before the pass closes. | Burned my paw on a pick head this morning.
b[smith] : Iron doesn't care about your paws. Gloves, pup.
b : Steady work. | They always do. | Ouch.
a : Too steady. | Always. | Ouch indeed.

scene rg_cb_lamp_wick
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : The tinker mended my lamp for a penny. Good as new. | A miner's lamp is worth more than his boots. | The tinker sells brass things nobody needs.
b[crafter] : A lamp that fails below is a grave. I mend them right.
b[miner] : Without my lamp I'm blind and buried.
b : Good deal. | True enough. | And people buy them.
a : Very good. | True. | They do.

scene rg_cb_shaft_collapse
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Another shaft fell in above the east mine. Nobody below, thank the Bright One. | The old workings under the town are hollow, they say. | My floor cracked last night. Under the town's all tunnels.
b[miner] : The mountain's honeycomb. One day the whole town'll sink.
b[old] : They mined under the crossroads a hundred years ago. Nobody wrote it down.
b : Thank the Bright One. | Probably. | Mine too.
a : Every day. | Probably. | Everyone's.

scene rg_cb_marches
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : The valley was all pine once, before the smelter. | Half the iron in Ridgemere's ironworks came down our pass. | Without Frosthollow ore, the city's forges would go cold.
b[old] : Pine to the snow line. My grandmother saw the last of it.
b[noble] : Frosthollow's ore keeps the city building. That is its honour.
b : Hard to imagine. | And they forget it. | They'd never say so.
a : Very hard. | Always. | Never.

scene rg_cb_pithead
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow here.place=street|market|work
a : The general store's out of candles. Again. | Stout boots at the store. Two marks. Two! | They give credit at the store till payday. Then they take it all.
b[merchant] : Candles go fastest in winter. Buy early, before the pass closes.
b : Again. | Robbery. | That's how it works.
a : Again. | Pure robbery. | Always.

scene rg_cb_iron_saint_feast
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow here.season=winter
a : On midwinter night the whole town walks the mine road with lamps. | They'll ring the chapel bell for every wolf below at midwinter. | No picks swing on midwinter day. Not one.
b[priest] : The Bright One walks with every miner. On the longest night, we walk with them.
b[miner] : Best day of the year. Nobody goes down.
b : Lovely sight. | Every year. | Not one.
a : Very lovely. | Every year. | Not one.

scene rg_cb_watchmen
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow a.role=guard
a : Two watchmen for a whole town of miners. It's a joke. | Broke up the fight at the Frozen Lantern. Got a black eye for it. | Somebody's stealing lamp oil from the store.
b[guard] : Two's enough when the miners keep their own peace. Mostly.
b : It is. | Earned it. | Probably a miner.
a : A bad one. | Every bit. | Probably.

scene rg_cb_slag_heap
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow a.stage=young|adolescent
a : We sledded down the slag heap on a board! | Found a shiny stone in the slag heap. | My mother says the slag heap's too dangerous.
b[old] : I slid down that heap when I was your age. Broke my tail.
b : Careful! | Let me see. | She's right.
a : I am careful! | It's pretty. | It's fun, though.

scene rg_cb_firedamp
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Bad air in the low drift today. Lamp flame went blue. | They lowered a bird down the new shaft. It came up fine. | The lamp's flame tells you everything below.
b[miner] : Blue flame, run. Don't stop for your pick.
b : Did you get out? | Good sign. | It does.
a : Fast. | Good sign. | Everything.

scene rg_cb_washday
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow here.place=home|street
a : Pointless doing the wash. It's grey by noon. | The stream's frozen again. Washing in melted snow. | We wash in the stream and come out dirtier.
b[old] : Grey snow, grey wolves. That's Frosthollow.
b : Do it anyway. | Every winter. | I know.
a : I do. | Every winter. | I know.

scene rg_cb_wages
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow a.job=miner|laborer
a : Payday's late. The buyer's cart hasn't come up the pass. | Wages in tokens again. The store takes them, at a discount. | We dug double this month and got the same pay.
b[miner] : The cart comes when the pass lets it.
b : Again? | Robbery. | Of course.
a : Again. | Robbery. | Of course.

scene rg_cb_hills_view
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : From the top workings you can see all the way down to Glasswater. | On a clear morning the lake flashes like a blade, all the way up here. | The world looks so clean from up here.
b[old] : From far away, everything looks clean.
b : A fine view. | Like a star. | It isn't.
a : Very fine. | It does. | Not at all.

scene rg_cb_tunnel_ghost
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : They say a miner still walks the old south drift, swinging his lamp. | Heard tapping in the dead workings again. | My lamp went out in the old drift and something breathed.
b[miner] : The knockers. Leave them bread and they warn you before a fall.
b[priest] : The dead rest. The living imagine.
b : Old tale. | Water dripping. | You imagined it.
a : Old and true. | Probably. | I didn't.

scene rg_cb_ore_carts
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow a.job=carter|laborer|miner
a : Ore carts down the pass all morning. | Brake broke on the icy bend. Cart went into the ditch. | The pass road's more holes than road.
b[carter] : Downhill on ice with a load of ore. Worst job in the Whitefangs.
b : Busy day. | Anybody hurt? | It always is.
a : Very busy. | Only the cart. | Always.

scene rg_cb_miners_wives
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow pair.band=friends|family|spouses
a : Every time the mine bell rings, my heart stops. | I wait at the shaft every evening till I see the lamp come up. | You never get used to waiting.
b[miner] : I count every evening I come up. Every one.
b : I know. | So do I. | Never.
a : I know. | Every evening. | Never.

scene rg_cb_iron_bread
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow here.place=home|tavern|street
a : Miners' pasties at the Frozen Lantern. Crust like armour. | My mother bakes the crust thick so you can hold it with sooty paws. | You throw the crust edge away, for the knockers.
b[miner] : Eat the middle, leave the crust. The knockers get hungry too.
b : Best food in the mountains. | Clever. | Old custom.
a : The best. | Very clever. | Very old.

scene fh_snowed_in
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.region=frosthollow here.weather=snow|storm
a : The pass is shut again. Snow to the shoulder. | Dug out the door twice this morning. | No carts down till the thaw.
b[carter] : I've turned back at the top bend three times this winter.
b[miner] : The mine's warmer than the street in this.
b : Again? | Only twice? | Beans till spring, then.
a : Again. | Twice. | Beans again.

scene fh_lord_up_the_pass
when topic=smalltalk|lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Lord Grayrock's coming up the pass to see the mines, they say. | Some great lord from Ridgemere's poking about the workings. | They swept the snow off the mine road. Lord Grayrock's due.
b[miner] : A lord in a mine. He'll want to see the seam and keep his boots clean.
b[old] : Lords come up, look at the hole, go back down. I've seen four.
b : In this cold? | Rather him than me. | For a lord, they sweep.
a : In this cold. | Me too. | Never for us.
